Subject: a candidate gives each candidacy as long as its grants take
Why: kiln's CP-T2.2 step 7: in Quiver's three-machine lab a leader's kill cost up to 113 terms; a candidate on a fast disk asked again before its voters, on a slow one, could make their votes durable and grant. Upstream as hyper-raft cp/t2.2-grant-wait (831bfd9, the test; d804110, the fix), offered for hyper-raft main.

